# Fibonacci in the mixin encoding of inheritance
# (corpora/contest_mixin_library.pl, the library `natural`): problems of
# the reduction series, ported from the retired labeled points of
# contest_inheritance_fibonacci.pl and contest_inheritance_middle_sizes.pl.
#
# THE SOURCE is the naive recursion `Fibonacci` of MIXINv2's
# FibonacciLibrary.mixin.yaml (MIXINv2/packages/mixinv2-examples/src/
# mixinv2_examples/): fibonacci(n) = fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2)
# for n > 1. The class fibonacci has the slots n and value, and is the
# one slot of a module of width 1, so that its value makes objects of the
# class read through the module's self, as the labeled port's
# `arithmetic / fibonacci`. value dispatches on self.n's accept and on
# self.n.predecessor's accept, which tell 0, 1 and more apart, and makes
# once = {fibonacci, n : self.n.predecessor} and
# twice = {fibonacci, n : self.n.predecessor.predecessor}, and answers
# once.value.plus(twice.value). The two recursive calls reach n - 2 by two
# spellings, the inner call's own n.predecessor and the outer call's
# n.predecessor.predecessor: equal values, different terms, so a reading
# that shares only equal spellings makes the naive recursion's calls,
# about the golden ratio a step.
#
# THE PROGRAM reads C.equality({fibonacci, n : K}.value) at church,
# the labeled program's check: fibonacci(8) = 21, fibonacci(10) = 55,
# fibonacci(12) = 144, fibonacci(14) = 377 (contest_inheritance_middle_sizes.pl),
# fibonacci(15) = 610, and the wrong fibonacci(10) == 56; and, smaller
# than the labeled family's, fibonacci(3) = 2 and fibonacci(4) = 3, so
# that the family has points weak_head reads.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT of each is the Boolean of the equation. PROOF:
# the recursion descends on the finite numeral n under every choice, every
# class has one implementation of each slot it is read at, and every end
# is the Boolean of the equation.
#
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#   fibonacci_point(?Point, ?Count, ?Claimed)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
λ
. cons
  ( λ _fibonacci_point
    . _fibonacci_point (text "reduction_mixin_fibonacci_three") (integer 3) λ. integer 2
  )
λ
. cons
  (λ_fibonacci_point. _fibonacci_point (text "reduction_mixin_fibonacci_four") (integer 4) λ. integer 3)
λ
. cons
  ( λ _fibonacci_point
    . _fibonacci_point (text "reduction_mixin_fibonacci_eight") (integer 8) λ. integer 21
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _fibonacci_point
    . _fibonacci_point (text "reduction_mixin_fibonacci_ten") (integer 10) λ. integer 55
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _fibonacci_point
    . _fibonacci_point (text "reduction_mixin_fibonacci_ten_wrong") (integer 10) λ. integer 56
  )
λ
